From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:01:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/48] net: xpon: omci: drop OMCI frames that fail the CRC

The baseline OMCI trailer carries a CRC-32 (G.984.4/G.988 message
format). A frame that fails it must be discarded so the OLT retransmits
it after its timeout.

The EN751221 and EN7523 receive paths flag such frames with
AIROHA_XPON_OAM_RX_F_CRC_ERROR, the glue turns that into
OMCI_F_CRC_ERROR and the core stores it in the skb control block, but
the agent never looked at it: any 44 or 48 byte frame was decoded and
executed. A corrupted Set or Create could apply wrong attribute values
under a valid TCI, or answer a TCI the OLT never sent; the clean
retransmission then missed the duplicate cache and ran again, returning
"instance exists" for a Create or counting a Set twice in MIB data sync.

Skip the agent for flagged frames, keep forwarding them to the netlink
observer with the flag, and count them in a new rx_crc_errors sysfs
attribute.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/core.c     | 11 ++++++++++-
 net/xpon/omci/internal.h |  1 +
 net/xpon/omci/sysfs.c    |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/core.c b/net/xpon/omci/core.c
index f97d43a..2e850bb 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/core.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/core.c
@@ -1185,7 +1185,16 @@ static void omci_rx_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		}
 		spin_unlock_bh(&odev->state_lock);
 
-		omci_agent_receive(odev, skb);
+		/*
+		 * The OMCI trailer carries a CRC-32: a frame that fails it is
+		 * discarded and the OLT retransmits it. Executing it would apply
+		 * whatever the corruption left and answer a TCI the OLT may never
+		 * have sent. The observer still gets it, with the flag.
+		 */
+		if (cb->flags & OMCI_F_CRC_ERROR)
+			atomic64_inc(&odev->rx_crc_errors);
+		else
+			omci_agent_receive(odev, skb);
 
 		mutex_lock(&odev->owner_lock);
 		if (odev->owner_portid && odev->owner_net) {
diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/internal.h b/net/xpon/omci/internal.h
index 4263609..37adfcc 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/internal.h
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/internal.h
@@ -194,6 +194,7 @@ struct omci_device {
 	atomic64_t rx_packets;
 	atomic64_t rx_bytes;
 	atomic64_t rx_dropped;
+	atomic64_t rx_crc_errors;
 	atomic64_t tx_packets;
 	atomic64_t tx_bytes;
 	atomic64_t tx_errors;
diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/sysfs.c b/net/xpon/omci/sysfs.c
index dea3323..d5999dd 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/sysfs.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/sysfs.c
@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@ static DEVICE_ATTR_RO(_name)
 OMCI_ATOMIC64_ATTR_RO(rx_packets, rx_packets);
 OMCI_ATOMIC64_ATTR_RO(rx_bytes, rx_bytes);
 OMCI_ATOMIC64_ATTR_RO(rx_dropped, rx_dropped);
+OMCI_ATOMIC64_ATTR_RO(rx_crc_errors, rx_crc_errors);
 OMCI_ATOMIC64_ATTR_RO(tx_packets, tx_packets);
 OMCI_ATOMIC64_ATTR_RO(tx_bytes, tx_bytes);
 OMCI_ATOMIC64_ATTR_RO(tx_errors, tx_errors);
@@ -685,6 +686,7 @@ static struct attribute *omci_attrs[] = {
 	&dev_attr_rx_packets.attr,
 	&dev_attr_rx_bytes.attr,
 	&dev_attr_rx_dropped.attr,
+	&dev_attr_rx_crc_errors.attr,
 	&dev_attr_tx_packets.attr,
 	&dev_attr_tx_bytes.attr,
 	&dev_attr_tx_errors.attr,
